# Files whose exact bytes matter must come out of a Windows checkout the same as
# on a Mac: git's line-ending conversion would change them. Git applies the LAST
# matching line, so the specific rule goes after the general one.

# Everything the app embeds and serves, so a Windows build ships the same files.
# "auto" keeps git's binary detection, so an image in there is left alone.
internal/adapters/httpapi/web/** text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored hls.js: its SHA-256 is checked by a test
# (internal/adapters/httpapi/static_hls_test.go). Never convert it.
internal/adapters/httpapi/web/hls.min.js -text

# The CI and release workflows run these under Git Bash on Windows, where a
# carriage return at the end of a line is a syntax error.
*.sh text eol=lf
